\f2 Yes. The Anstey procedure is importantly different from what Kathy has been doing so far, and it gives you exactly the distinction you want.\
Kathy\'92s first-week work is mainly asking:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 Is Chilli present, and how much of it is present?
\f2\b0 \
Her blood/respiratory testing and payload-specific PCR can detect Chilli circulating as virus, inside cells, or as viral genetic material. None of that means Chilli has become part of the host genome.\
Anstey is asking a different question:\

\f3\b Has TPlus become physically incorporated into a human chromosome?
\f2\b0 \
That is why she:\
prepared the tissue, isolated the DNA and loaded the sample\
and then explicitly used:\

\f3\b FIND HOST JUNCTIONS
\f2\b0 \
The decisive result is not merely finding TPlus sequence. It is finding:\

\f3\b human DNA 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f3  complete TPlus construct 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f3  human DNA
\f2\b0 \
inside one continuous chromosome.\
So you can cleanly maintain:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Ordinary Chilli-positive Elvi:
\f2\b0  Chilli is present in their bodies/cells and can be measured at different concentrations, but when their 
\f3\b host DNA
\f2\b0  is examined there are no human\'96Chilli junctions.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Chanta:
\f2\b0  Chilli is also detectable conventionally, but examination of his 
\f3\b host DNA
\f2\b0  shows the complete construct embedded between human sequences.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 That makes Chanta categorically different rather than merely \'93having more Chilli\'94.\
And importantly, your existing first movement does 
\f3\b not
\f2\b0  require Kathy to have already discovered this. When you wrote:\
\'93sequencing showed high-titre viral material\'94\
and then payload-specific PCR screening, that can straightforwardly mean she was identifying and quantifying the viral material in her samples. She was not performing Anstey\'92s specific 
\f3\b host-junction analysis
\f2\b0 .\
So there is no contradiction between:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 Week one:
\f2\b0  Kathy knows Chilli is in certain Elvi.\
and:\

\f3\b Post-Humpenings:
\f2\b0  Kathy discovers that Chilli is 
\f5\i in Chanta\'92s chromosomes
\f2\i0 .\
The Anstey scene actually gives you a very economical established vocabulary for the latter. You don't need to invent any new sequencing procedure around Kathy. The important conceptual distinction is simply 
\f3\b detecting the construct versus finding host junctions
\f2\b0 .\
